    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=6,\\ b=5$.\n\nUse $f(-1)=3$, then match the branch values at $x=1$.",
      "worked": "Since $-1<1$, use the branch $f(x)=2x+b$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2(-1)+b&=3\\\\b&=5\\end{align*}$$\nAt the breakpoint $x=1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}f(1)&=1+a\\\\f_L(1)&=2+5\\\\f_L(1)&=7\\\\f_R(1)&=1+a\\end{align*}$$\nContinuity requires all three values to agree:\n$$\\begin{align*}1+a&=7\\\\a&=6\\end{align*}$$\nEach branch is a polynomial, so it is continuous throughout its interval. With $a=6$ and $b=5$, all three boundary values equal $7$, so $f$ is continuous throughout its domain.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
